      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Prajwal Tomar</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/PrajwalTomar_">@PrajwalTomar_</a>)</p><blockquote><p>Builders running only Claude Code are about to get lapped by the ones running Hermes alongside it.<br/><br/>While you're re-explaining your stack in every new Claude session, they're running 4 specialized Hermes agents 24/7 on a $5 VPS. Chief of Staff. Head of Research. Head of Content. Head of Finance.<br/><br/>Each one has its own SOUL .md identity, its own memory, and writes its own skills after every task.<br/><br/>The agent paradigm just split in two:<br/><br/>→ Session-based agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex) win focused coding sessions<br/>→ Persistent agents (Hermes) win everything around the coding (research, ops, content, scheduling)<br/><br/>(full breakdown in the article)</p></blockquote><div><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKsacz6aAAAY1El.jpg" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/></div><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 71 · 🔁 4 · 💬 8 · 🔖 99</p><p><a href="https://x.com/PrajwalTomar_/status/2065773939520119040">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
