## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKmhMxOW0AAWMPI?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/rewind02/article/2065412916858241404/media/2065359144870137856) How To Sell AI Agents To Local Businesses (and charge $15K+ for it) [![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2036190950545084416/aHeLH6m__normal.jpg)](http://x.com/rewind02) [rewind](http://x.com/rewind02)...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>rewind</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/rewind02">@rewind02</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/1806814090246893569">http://x.com/i/article/1806814090246893569</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/1806814090246893569">http://x.com/i/article/1806814090246893569</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKmhMxOW0AAWMPI?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/rewind02/article/2065412916858241404/media/2065359144870137856)<br/>How To Sell AI Agents To Local Businesses (and charge $15K+ for it)<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2036190950545084416/aHeLH6m__normal.jpg)](http://x.com/rewind02)<br/>[rewind](http://x.com/rewind02)<br/>[@rewind02](http://x.com/rewind02)<br/>·<br/>21h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow rewind02<br/>8<br/>14<br/>62<br/>[21K](http://x.com/rewind02/status/2065412916858241404/analytics)<br/>You don't need a portfolio. You don't need a team. You don't need years of sales experience or a business degree What you need is one thing: the ability to solve a problem that local business owners have right now and will pay serious money to fix Agencies are now charging anywhere from $15,000 to $25,000+ upfront per client, not even including the recurring monthly revenue The reason this works is simple: business owners don’t care how the system is built They only care about one thing: more leads, more appointments, more closed deals If you can deliver that, the technical side is irrelevant to them This guide breaks down exactly how to sell AI agents to local businesses, from picking your niche to running the sales call to delivering results Let's get into it<br/>## <br/>1\. Why local businesses are your best customer<br/>Most people who get into AI go after the wrong customers They try to sell to people who already have engineering teams and in-house developers Those customers don't need you, they already have someone A real estate agent, a roofer, an HVAC company, a med spa - these businesses are run by people who are exceptional at their trade and have no idea how to implement technology They're looking for someone who can solve a specific, painful problem they've been dealing with for years - They need more leads - They need those leads to turn into booked appointments - They need those appointments to close into paying customers Most of them are either doing this manually, paying for marketing that only addresses one of the three, or losing leads every day because nobody followed up fast enough The gap between where they are and where they need to be is worth serious money to them<br/>Why they're willing to payLocal businesses operate on clear, measurable economics A roofing job pays $10,000\. If your system books them three extra jobs a month, that's $30,000 in additional revenue A $1,500 monthly fee to keep that system running is an obvious decision - that's a 20x return<br/>Most local businesses could increase their annual revenue by at least $30,000 with a better sales process alone What they haven't had is someone who can actually build it for themWhy the timing is right<br/>AI voice agents are improving faster than most people realize<br/>They're replacing front desk roles, handling inbound calls, setting appointments 24 hours a day without sick days or payroll A year ago this technology wasn't good enough for production use with real clients. Now it is<br/>The businesses that figure this out first will have a significant advantage over their competitors Most of them know AI is coming - they just don't know how to implement it<br/>That's the entire value proposition. You're selling the outcome that software produces, to people who have the money to pay for it and the problem to justify it<br/>## <br/>2\. Why other online business models don't work<br/>Before we get into how to sell AI agents, it's worth understanding why most people who try to make money online fail Not because they're lazy or unmotivated - because they pick models that are structurally brokenWeb design agenciesWeb design used to be a legitimate business Then AI tools got good enough to build a decent website in an hour, and platforms like Fiverr flooded the market with freelancers charging $50 to $100 for the same work The moment you quote them $1,500</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 73 · 🔁 13 · 💬 10 · 🔖 135</p><p><a href="https://x.com/rewind02/status/2065412916858241404">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
