      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>The Startup Ideas Podcast (SIP) 🧃</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/startupideaspod">@startupideaspod</a>)</p><blockquote><p>The reason your AI gives generic answers isn't the model.<br/><br/>It's that your company's knowledge lives in 12 different tools and your agent can't see any of it.<br/><br/>So here's how to build a context database your agents can actually use:<br/><br/>1) Pull it in:<br/>- Slack, email, meetings, docs, tickets<br/>- Auto-collected on a schedule into one place.<br/><br/>2) Clean it up.<br/>- An agent files what matters and drops the noise, so your brain doesn't bloat.<br/><br/>3) Store it as memory.<br/>- Folders of files your agents read from and write back to as they learn.<br/><br/>4) Point your agents at it.<br/>- Now they draft, build, and ship with full context instead of guessing.<br/><br/>Same model. Same agent.<br/><br/>The difference is whether it can understand your company or not.<br/><br/>Build the database once. <br/><br/>Everything downstream gets smarter.</p></blockquote><div><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2065514387893600256/img/aWeKlaBBPUviqXSC.jpg" alt="" style="max-width:480px;margin:4px"/></div><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 76 · 🔁 7 · 💬 8 · 🔖 129</p><p><a href="https://x.com/startupideaspod/status/2065516731691581922">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
