      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>James Shields</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/scaling_shields">@scaling_shields</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062498846085685248">http://x.com/i/article/2062498846085685248</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2062498846085685248">http://x.com/i/article/2062498846085685248</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKkd3r1XcAAjYZW?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/scaling%5Fshields/article/2065491111003746412/media/2065214746622652416)<br/>the most valuable article on agency client acquisition EVER created<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1978439762731020290/iNWmGYro_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/scaling%5Fshields)<br/>[James Shields](http://x.com/scaling%5Fshields)<br/>[@scaling\_shields](http://x.com/scaling%5Fshields)<br/>·<br/>16h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow scaling\_shields<br/>2<br/>10<br/>38<br/>[4.2K](http://x.com/scaling%5Fshields/status/2065491111003746412/analytics)<br/>most agency owners get clients the same three ways: - referrals - content - and praying lol<br/>ALL three share one problem. you do not control the tap<br/>cold email is the only channel where you decide how many shots you take tomorrow. <br/>that's the entire reason it beats everything else for an agency, and almost nobody runs it properly.<br/>this is why it wins, and exactly how to run it...<br/>## <br/>why cold email beats everything for agencies:<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKkb2ipXsAEyNt6?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/scaling%5Fshields/article/2065491111003746412/media/2065212527953293313)<br/>referrals are lovely until they dry up, and they ALWAYS dry up because they depend on other people remembering you exist. <br/>content compounds beautifully and takes a year before it pays you a cent. <br/>paid ads work and bleed you the entire time you're learning them<br/>cold email is just math you control. you want more calls next week, send more emails next week<br/>it's linear and it's in your hands, which none of the others ones are<br/>run the numbers. send 100,000 emails in a month. half a percent reply positive, that's 500 interested people. <br/>book 20% of them, that's 100 calls. close 15%, that's 15 clients. at a $2,500 ticket that's $37k that month, <br/>and that's the deliberately CONSERVATIVE version. <br/>the only two inputs are volume and an offer that doesn't suck. <br/>really simple<br/>## <br/>how to actually set it up:<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKkcAzMXkAApq5H?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/scaling%5Fshields/article/2065491111003746412/media/2065212704193744896)<br/>infrastructure comes first and it IS NOT optional. <br/>you need inboxes, a lot of them, because you send 25 emails a day per inbox to stay safe. <br/>300 inboxes gets you 4,500 a day. you warm every one of them for 14 days before they send a thing, no shortcuts, or you torch your deliverability on day one. <br/>you send from subdomains, never your main domain, so if something burns it isn't your actual website lmfao<br/>then the offer, because it carries the WHOLE campaign. <br/>a mediocre email with an insane offer beats a beautiful email with an average offer every single time because nobody gives a shit about your clever copy, <br/>they care about the offer. <br/>you need to make it so clear a tired mf gets it in like five seconds<br/>then leads, and this is where most people lose. <br/>please DO NOT pull the same broad apollo list ten thousand other agencies are hammering. <br/>scrape where nobody else is looking and where the market isn't saturated<br/>## <br/>the levers that separate 1 call from 100:<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKkcPofW0AE1IR5?format=jpg&amp;name=small)](http://x.com/scaling%5Fshields/article/2065491111003746412/media/2065212959018635265)<br/>volume first, because it's the cheat code everyone's scared of (if you can't tell already, i LOVE volume)<br/>200 emails a day is a hobby. <br/>the people winning are sending THOUSANDS a day, looking spammy doing it, and not caring, because they're booked out while you protect your reputation into the ground and book zero calls<br/>then reply speed. <br/>every positive reply gets answered in under ten minutes and warm called on the phone while they're still warm. <br/>this one habit will roughly double your booked calls off the exact same replies. <br/>then</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 46 · 🔁 10 · 💬 3 · 🔖 118</p><p><a href="https://x.com/scaling_shields/status/2065491111003746412">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
