## To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark [View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts) [![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKfvJxpbsAA9ULp?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/mvanhorn/article/2064887887578136666/media/2064881905397641216) /Last1Day of Fable 5: Best Practices and the Funniest Things People Are Saying [![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1565403341647400960/55RW_HGX_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/mvanhorn) [Matt Van Horn](http://x.com/mvanhorn)...</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Matt Van Horn</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/mvanhorn">@mvanhorn</a>)</p><blockquote><p><a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064864205749280768">http://x.com/i/article/2064864205749280768</a></p></blockquote><hr/><p>🔗 <a href="http://x.com/i/article/2064864205749280768">http://x.com/i/article/2064864205749280768</a></p><blockquote>## <br/>To view keyboard shortcuts, press question mark<br/>[View keyboard shortcuts](http://x.com/i/keyboard%5Fshortcuts)<br/>[![Image](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HKfvJxpbsAA9ULp?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900)](http://x.com/mvanhorn/article/2064887887578136666/media/2064881905397641216)<br/>/Last1Day of Fable 5: Best Practices and the Funniest Things People Are Saying<br/>[![](https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1565403341647400960/55RW_HGX_normal.jpg)](http://x.com/mvanhorn)<br/>[Matt Van Horn](http://x.com/mvanhorn)<br/>[@mvanhorn](http://x.com/mvanhorn)<br/>·<br/>5h<br/>Follow<br/>Click to Follow mvanhorn<br/>8<br/>6<br/>109<br/>[10K](http://x.com/mvanhorn/status/2064887887578136666/analytics)<br/>Fable 5 is one day old. I ran <br/>[/last30days](https://github.com/mvanhorn/last30days-skill/)<br/> on it five times, 865 items across Reddit, X, YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, Hacker News, and Polymarket, while running the model myself the whole time. Here's what survived day one: the best practices, with receipts, and the funniest things the internet said.<br/>## <br/>1\. Give It a Harder Job Than You Think You Should<br/>The official playbook is two words: aim higher. Hand Fable 5 tasks harder than what you gave prior models, let it interview you before executing, and strip the over-prescriptive scaffolding out of your old prompts, because the numbered babysitting steps now degrade output. I tested this on day one and it's real. State the outcome, get out of the way. And never ask it to echo its internal reasoning, which trips refusals per the official guide.<br/>Which makes the funniest comment of the launch even better. On <br/>[Alex Finn's](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RwsUnvHYmyw)<br/> "I'm speechless" video (115K views in a day), <br/>[151 likes](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RwsUnvHYmyw)<br/>:<br/>&gt; Buddy said it's a mythos level model then proceeded to create a todo app and a snake game like a good boy<br/>&gt; \- mousepaddd, YouTube<br/>Everyone got told to aim higher. Everyone made a snake game.<br/>## <br/>2\. Set Goals, Not Steps<br/>The biggest workflow change in the corpus: stop walking the model through tasks and start stating destinations. <br/>[Anthropic's own Claude Code team](https://di.gg/ai/zrppa6ui)<br/> says Fable 5 moved their work "from micro-managing tasks to high-level goal alignment," with a new /goal command for continuous operation.<br/>One catch, per <br/>[Simon Willison's](https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/9/claude-fable-5/)<br/> "slow, expensive and capable" review: it often keeps working until stopped. Write a hard stop rule into every long run, a budget cap, a time cap, or a done condition.<br/>The community immediately found the logical endpoint:<br/>&gt; /goal make 1 million dollars, make no mistake<br/>&gt; \- FreqtradeFR, YouTube, <br/>&gt; <br/>&gt; [92 likes](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RwsUnvHYmyw)<br/>## <br/>3\. Run It as an Orchestrator, Not a Worker<br/>Everyone landed on the same architecture within 24 hours. <br/>[@Steve8708](https://x.com/@Steve8708)<br/>'s <br/>[verdict](https://x.com/Steve8708/status/2064847457977319735)<br/>: Fable is "a step smarter than GPT 5.5 and Opus" and "needs less babysitting than any other model out there," but "slow and expensive as hell - best used as an orchestrator of cheaper models." <br/>[@aplomb2](https://x.com/@aplomb2)<br/>'s routing: <br/>[Fable plans, Sonnet implements, Haiku tests](https://x.com/aplomb2/status/2064838222014984228)<br/>. Half your agents build, half verify, and the verify pass gates the commit.<br/>The launch receipt is absurd on its own: Stripe pointed Fable 5 at a 50-million-line Ruby codebase and shipped a one-day migration a full team had scoped at two months, per <br/>[Anthropic's own announcement](https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-fable-5-mythos-5)<br/>.<br/>And the <br/>[definitive write-up](https://x.com/amirmxt/status/2064852788799062308)<br/> of what happens if you skip the routing advice:<br/>&gt; "mom how did we get so poor?" "your dad ran claude fable 5 subagent workflows with no spend limit"<br/>&gt; \- <br/>&gt; <br/>&gt; [@amirmxt](https://x.com/@amirmxt)<br/>## <br/>4\. Work the Effort Dial, Medium Is the Sleeper<br/>Effort</blockquote><p style="color:#777;font-size:0.9em">♥ 245 · 🔁 24 · 💬 13 · 🔖 477</p><p><a href="https://x.com/mvanhorn/status/2064887887578136666">View on X →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
